  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Ty France supplied two runs when the lineup finally needed them, and the Padres held a one-run lead from the third inning onward against Atlanta.",
    "what_this_means": "JP Sears gave them six strong innings. 5 hits, 2 runs, 5 strikeouts. Which meant the game stayed tight all night. France's early power set the tone. The offense wasn't lavish. Seven hits and eight strikeouts suggested a lineup working against itself, not clicking. But the bullpen didn't blink. David Morgan threw 1.1 scoreless innings. Wandy Peralta pitched a clean frame. Jason Adam closed it out. This is what a three-run win looks like when nothing is wasted: a starter who eats innings, a reliever corps that doesn't give ground, and enough from the bats to hold the line. The Padres are now 3-0 in their last three games because they stopped trying to blow games open and started accepting that narrow margins work.",
